## Requirements

- Python 3.10+
- An OpenAI-compatible vision model endpoint, e.g. [LM Studio](https://lmstudio.ai) with a
  vision model downloaded (tested: `google/gemma-4-e4b`, `google/gemma-4-12b`)

## Install

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd Handwriting_Transcription
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate            # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e ".[test]"            # package + jiwer for scoring
pip install gradio                  # only needed for the demo
```

## Install as a package (use only)

```bash
pip install git+https://github.com/<user>/<repo>.git
```

Then in any Python code:

```python
from handwriting_transcription import image_to_text, TranscriptionError
```

## Configure

Edit `src/llm_transcription_config.yaml`:

```yaml
model:
    id: google/gemma-4-e4b                              # model to use
    chat_url: http://localhost:1234/v1/chat/completions # your endpoint
    temperature: 1.0
    timeout: 300

preprocess: false    # true = grayscale, contrast, binarize, remove lines
```

For testing and the demo, edit `src/models.yaml` (models to compare, LM Studio base URL, context length).

## Usage

### As a module

```python
from handwriting_transcription import image_to_text
with open("page.png", "rb") as f:
    result = image_to_text(f.read())                     # uses the config's model
print(result["choices"][0]["message"]["content"])
```

Override the model or temperature per call:

```python
result = image_to_text(image_bytes, "google/gemma-3-12b", 0.2)
```

Accepts any image format Pillow reads (PNG, JPEG, TIFF...). Raises `TranscriptionError` on request failures.

### Run a test on CVL data

Requires the CVL data (see **Test data**). From the project root:

```bash
python -m src.test_llm_transcription 10 42      # 10 random pages, seed 42
```

Results go to `runs/<timestamp>/`: `images/`, `targets/`, `outputs/<model>/`, `seed.txt`, and `scores.csv` (CER/WER per model and image).

### Run the demo

```bash
python demo.py
```

Opens a Gradio page on port 7860 with webcam/upload, model selection and temperature. With `share=True` (set in `demo.py`), it also prints a public `*.gradio.live` link.

## Test data (CVL)

The CVL Database is not included (license: CC BY-NC 3.0, non-commercial research only).

1. Download from https://zenodo.org/records/1492267:
   `cvl-database-1-1.zip` and `cvl-database-cropped-1-1.zip`
2. Extract both into `data/`:

   data/
   ├── cvl-database-1-1/          # trainset/ and testset/ with xml ground truth
   └── cvl-database-cropped-1-1/  # handwriting-only page images

3. Run a test: `python -m src.test_llm_transcription <num_images> <seed>`

